/* Cross-ISO mechanism matrix — SPP shard (rule 28 [R-MECH-MATRIX]).
 *
 * This file is SPP's COLUMN of the matrix: one line per mechanism id
 * (the row set lives in ../mechanism-matrix.js, which carries the
 * mechanism-level id/cat/name/def/mode/note). A session that tests a
 * mechanism in SPP updates ONLY this file — the cell verdict, the
 * forecast-lane posture (fc), the evidence citation (ev) and any
 * SPP-specific note — plus the keeper/gates stamps on promotion.
 * Never edit another ISO's shard (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]): a verdict
 * transfers to no other ISO; candidates enter the target shard as U.
 *
 * Cell codes (same vocabulary as the base header): K keeper, R rejected,
 * I inert, G governance-refused/closed, O open, U untested, . n/a.
 * `fc` is the forecast-lane posture where it DIFFERS from the backcast
 * cell (omitted = same as cell). `ev` is this ISO's evidence citation.
 *
 * SEEDED AT SPP-21 (2026-09-06), the seventh shard — mechanical emission,
 * NO VERDICT MINTED. SPP has no keeper, no registered run and no solve of
 * any kind at HEAD, so `keeper` and `gates` are deliberately EMPTY and every
 * cell is `U` (untested, plausibly applicable) or `.` (structurally n/a).
 * Charter: docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §5 row SPP-21 (the
 * W5 lever queue it seeds is §4 there and docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md
 * §5.7); record docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-21-2026-09-06.md.
 *
 * THE CLASSIFICATION RULE, applied in order (so a later lane can audit any
 * cell without re-deriving the whole column):
 *   (a) ISO-EXCLUSIVE ELSEWHERE -> `.` — the row names another ISO's own
 *       market object (a foreign ScenarioConfig field stem, or a foreign
 *       region/programme name: wtx_ path15_ wecc_ tsa_ rdt_tcdc) AND no
 *       non-owner ISO has entered the cell at HEAD. A foreign-stemmed row
 *       that some OTHER ISO HAS entered is a live cross-ISO question, so
 *       SPP reads `U` there, not `.` (e.g. ercot_wind_zone_shape,
 *       miso_intermediate_gas_offer_margin, pjm_midcurve_belt).
 *   (b) NO CENTRALIZED FORWARD CAPACITY AUCTION -> `.` — the object is a
 *       cleared capacity price, its VRR/FCA/RBDC or locality demand curve,
 *       its sell-offer-stack clearing, its published default-ACR offer-cap
 *       convention, or its net-CONE vintages. SPP is energy-only with a
 *       bilateral RA obligation. SIX rows: capacity_market_clearing,
 *       capacity_market_supply_clearing, capacity_going_forward_bar_published,
 *       capacity_no_default_cap_convention, net_cone_forward_vintages,
 *       locality_capacity_curves.
 *   (c) NO CARBON PROGRAMME -> `.` — the object is a state/regional carbon
 *       programme (RGGI / CA cap-and-trade); no state in SPP's footprint
 *       carries one. ONE row: state_carbon_pricing.
 *   otherwise -> `U`.
 * `.` is the STRONGER claim (it forecloses a lever), so every row this
 * session could not place with a stated structural reason falls through to
 * `U`, the weaker one — including rows whose applicability is genuinely open
 * (capacity_deliverability, reserve_margin_backstop,
 * capacity_adequacy_requirement_published, adequacy_internal_supply_accounting,
 * lcr_tsl_published, m2m_seam_entitlement_cap, mass_cap_lp_row, legacy_p2).
 * A later SPP lane closes those on SPP's own data (rule 25), never by
 * reading another column.
 * Forecast-only rows (base `mode: "F"`) carry `cell: "."` — a forecast
 * mechanism has no backcast posture — plus `fc: "U"` where applicable. SPP
 * has NO forecast-lane entry at HEAD: that is W6 / SPP-60, gated and routed
 * to the capx director (plan §3 card P8), and this shard is not the forecast
 * board.
 *
 * Owner rulings already reflected in this seed: P4 (r#2, 2026-09-06) —
 * reserve co-optimisation is DEFERRED, cells `U`, SPP-56 queued last.
 *
 * Append SPP column re-stamp history as block comments at the END of this
 * file.
 */
