    measured_ramp_capability: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7. SPP-73 (2026-09-22, zero LP, RESULT-spp-73-commitment-reach-2026-09-22.md): STILL U, NOT TESTED, but BOUNDED for C3a/C3b — SPP's own DA unit commitment priced the RT top-88 hours at a median $26.9 vs RT $144.4 and model $23.7 (2020), closing 2.6 % / 4.5 % / 14.9 % of the gap in 2020 / 2019 / 2022; CAMPD SWPP-BA gas commitment state in those hours already matches the model's (CT x1.47 measured vs x1.32 model into the spike); no published per-class SPP start-up cost exists. A successor proposing this cell for the rung's price rows must first beat the DA bound (phi >= 0.5). SPP-81 (2026-09-25, cell NOT moved -- stays U; ZERO LP): RTBM cleared ramp-up / uncertainty MW now landed hourly 2019-2025 (data/raw/_validation-source/spp_rtbm_or_cleared_hourly.parquet). Within 2-GW net-load bins cleared ramp-up MW has a NEGATIVE, noise-level coefficient on MEC/delivered gas (-0.05 to -0.18 HR per 100 MW, |r| <= 0.07); the ramp product was live all of Mar-Dec 2022 with residual -0.09 HR; the 2023 step begins April, before the uncertainty product (2023-07-06); uncertainty MW peaked in 2025 (781 MW) when the residual was smallest. Ramp/uncertainty procurement does not carry the upper-tercile object. Evidence: docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-81-residual-upper-tercile-2026-09-25.md section 4. SPP-81b (2026-09-25, cell NOT moved -- stays U; ZERO LP; docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-81-upper-tercile-residual-2026-09-25.md s.3): the upper tercile's hours did NOT shift into the post-solar evening ramp (HE17-21 share 27.3 / 30.7 / 28.7 / 30.1 / 28.9 %, 2019/20/23/24/25), so ramp or commitment of peakers cannot own the 2023-24 object on timing grounds. The commitment/bridge cells stay R (no new evidence). Open sub-hourly candidate: five-minute ramp-limited intervals (s.6 item 2). SPP-82 (2026-09-25, cell NOT moved -- stays U; ZERO LP; docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-82-offered-not-setting-2026-09-25.md s.3): five-minute MEC (rtbm-lmp-by-location) in the sampled upper-tercile hours: hourly mean - interval median rose $0.8/1.3 -> $2.5/2.5 (~$1.5 of a $14-17 level), and at the interval median the offer-stack position still steps 0.656/0.648 -> 0.762/0.792 (+0.125/+0.136 vs +0.12/+0.15 at the mean). Ramp-limited intervals carry ~8-10 % of the object, and rule 8 keeps the model hourly regardless." },
