    st_gas_mustrun_p25: { cell: "K", fc: "U", ev: "PROMOTED 2026-09-10 BY OWNER RULING (verbatim: 'Is this a recommended keeper candidate? If so plz promote. If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper.') \u2014 K: the host flag st_gas_mustrun_per_plant is ARMED ON SPP's DESIGNATED KEEPER 2026-09-10-spp-64-stgas-selfcommit (eighth SPP keeper, over keeper 7 2026-09-10-spp-62-vintage-census). st_gas_mustrun_p25_level REMAINS FALSE and refused on rule 25. SPP-64 (2026-09-10, span solved and REGISTERED as 2026-09-10-spp-64-stgas-selfcommit; docs/RESULT-spp64-span.md, charter docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-spp-64-stgas-selfcommit-2026-09-10.md, screen docs/handoffs/RESULT-spp64-screen-2023.md) \u2014 THE HOST FLAG st_gas_mustrun_per_plant IS TESTED AND ARMED IN A REGISTERED SPP RUN; st_gas_mustrun_p25_level IS NOT ARMED AND WAS REFUSED EX ANTE (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]: its rationale is MISO's own out-of-market VLR record \u2014 Entergy South, Amite South / DSG / WOTAB \u2014 and SPP has no equivalent driver; the LEVEL used is committed_pct, the P5-of-online LSL, which is the SMALLEST of the three the artifact offers: 9.090 TWh all-on vs p25_cf 14.427 and median_cf 23.319). The lane REGISTERED WITHOUT PROMOTING and recommended promotion; the owner then RULED to promote in-session and this cell moved O -> K. DRIVER (rule 17 [R-FLOOR-WINDOW] triple): SPP's gas-steam fleet is 100.0 % EIA-860 Sector 1 'Electric Utility' \u2014 9,515 of 9,515 MW, zero IPP \u2014 so it self-commits to native load rather than making a merchant start/stop decision against the LMP; the reading is NOT vacuous, the same census reads CC_REGULAR 68.9 % Sector 1 and CT_PEAKER 99.7 %. WINDOW: each plant's own measured online_frac (0.286-0.954, mean 0.518) placed in the top round(online_frac x 8760) hours ranked by THE MODEL'S OWN system load \u2014 not the meter's on/off record (the form SPP-46 declared INADMISSIBLE) and not the P0 pattern (the form SPP-44 killed), which is why this is SPP-44's own stated re-test condition and not a re-arm. Rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH] machine-verified on the SOLVED artifact, not just pre-solve: ST_GAS was 0.0 % forced and absent from the keeper's D-2 entirely, and in the arm every other class stays 0.0 % forced. Rule 21 [R-DOF]: ZERO free parameters added, ledger inherited at n_entries 3 / n_residual 2; offer_curve_by_group byte-identical. MEASURED (span 2023/2024/2025, ONE --years invocation, 12 min 5 s, control = the keeper's COMMITTED bundle differenced per rule 29(b) form 4, no control solve): ST_GAS gross +2.3314 / +2.2886 / +2.5736 TWh, paid by COAL_PRB, CC_REGULAR and CT_PEAKER, NOT by curtailing wind (-0.0150 / -0.0106 / -0.0071); energy conserved to +0.0009 / -0.0013 / -0.0008 TWh; slack and dump BYTE-IDENTICAL to the keeper (dump 0, slack 0 / 370.102 / 0 MWh). SCORER: determination NOT-YET -> CALIBRATED, grade 6/8 -> 7/8, 2 fails -> 0 fails, 1 ledgered caveat; C1 FAIL -> PASS with BOTH failing rows closing on volume AND share (2023 ST_GAS -8.380 -> -6.034 TWh, share_pp -2.94 -> -2.12; 2024 -9.712 -> -7.423, -3.34 -> -2.55), free-class C1 14/16 all / 10/12 free -> 16/16 / 12/12; C2 gas 'C1 flags: ST_GAS' -> all classes in band; C3a +2.1/+1.3/+2.2 % -> +1.0/+0.1/+0.7 %; C3b 0.172/0.172/0.167 -> 0.173/0.171/0.163; C4 improves in 5 of 6 rows; C8 PASS. THE DETERMINATION FLIP IS C1'S ALONE \u2014 C3c is UNCHANGED at full magnitude (0 / 5 / 0 model hours >$200 against 42 / 59 / 68 actual, system price max byte-identical) and merely reclassified to a ledgered CAVEAT by rule 22 [R-C3C]'s standing rule once it became the LONE failure; SPP's absent tail (R-bd) is exactly as absent as before. 2025 C1 is SKIPPED for every class (preliminary EIA-923), so the C1 verdict rests on 2023-2024. THE ADVERSE FINDING, REPORTED NOT ABSORBED \u2014 D-4 PER-UNIT CONDUCT RIDER FAILS IN ALL THREE YEARS (4 / 5 / 3 rows; the keeper carried ZERO), flipping D4.passed True -> False: plants 1230, 1235 and 1271 fail in EVERY year with measured median 0.000 MW over the hours the floor binds for them and 59-83 % of those hours metered at zero (3008 in 2023-24, 6193 in 2024). That is rule 17's signature at the per-unit grain \u2014 'a floor binding in hours its own driver evidence says the class is offline is a bug by definition' \u2014 and it is a WINDOW-CONSTRUCTION defect: the top-system-load placement is verified by the meter for 15/19, 15/20 and 17/20 plants and FALSIFIED for the rest. Magnitude 0.0595 / 0.0763 / 0.0216 TWh = 2.56 / 3.26 / 0.85 % of the mechanism's forced energy. THE CLASS-LEVEL D-4 WINDOW LEG PASSES (offwindow_share 0.0000, self-windowing h0-23), and CRITICALLY THE RIDER NEVER REACHED THE DETERMINATION: calibration_verdict._score_forced_share consults _d4_provenance ONLY for a class ABOVE its cap, and ST_GAS came in UNDER \u2014 rule 20 [R-FORCED-BUDGET] forced share 0.1962 / 0.1849 / 0.1744 against d2_merchant_max_share 0.30 (ST_GAS is NOT in d2_exempt_classes, so this is a real test), so C8 passed on the share alone and the CALIBRATED headline was produced by a code path that never examined this defect. The PRECOMMIT's pre-declared ~0.33 forced-share risk did NOT materialise, so the rule's conditional-pass limb was never reached and the 'is a 100 %-regulated class a MERCHANT class' question is LEFT OPEN rather than answered. D-1 passes comfortably and IMPROVES: profile_r 0.997 / 0.999 / 0.997 (bar 0.80) and cv_ratio 2.117 / 1.844 / 1.717 moving TOWARD 1.0 from the keeper's 2.161 / 2.060 / 2.244 (bar 0.50, one-sided, so the improvement earns nothing). LANE RECOMMENDS PROMOTION on rule-1 structural grounds (the incumbent gives a 100 %-regulated fleet NO commitment structure at all, so the choice is 'right on ~80 % of the fleet vs right on none of it', and reverting trades a 2.3 TWh structural repair for a 0.02-0.08 TWh defect) WITH the window defect opened as the immediate successor card and NOT absorbed; it is explicitly NOT a mustrun_plant_exclusions job as a first reach (miso-170's own warning: excluding a conduct-test failure 'would bury that error inside a membership list'). Clean-first alternative costed at ~12 min of LP. [R-HOLDOUT] removed 2026-09-09, so every year here is model-SELECTION evidence and CALIBRATED is a rubric determination, NOT a certified out-of-sample skill claim. DO-NOT-REDO: st_gas_mustrun_p25_level stays REFUSED for SPP on rule 25; do not re-test the CAMPD-online-hours window (SPP-46 INADMISSIBLE) or the P0-anchored form (SPP-44)." },
