    unit_outage_short_windows_gas: { cell: "R", ev: "Row added by pjm-d4-4 (2026-09-10) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): a verdict is strictly per-ISO and PJM\u0027s does not fill this cell \u2014 no parameter transfers, since the scope carries none. The transfer question is cheap, zero-LP and well-posed: derive this ISO\u0027s own gas sub-5-day family (--short-windows --short-window-groups gas --merit-order-guard), measure its annual-mean and event-hour MW against this ISO\u0027s own published forced/planned composition gap, and check the per-stratum correlation sign against this ISO\u0027s own published FORCED series before proposing anything. An ISO whose gas fleet is small, or whose published record is not typed, may find the family immaterial or the identification unavailable. MOVED U -> R by SPP-32 (2026-09-12): REJECTED for SPP on two pre-registered gates, and this is a rule 28(d) NON-TRANSFER demonstrated rather than asserted. SPP had no gas extract, so one was derived from SPP's OWN CAMPD record with an invocation BYTE-IDENTICAL to PJM's committed sidecar on every knob (fullstop_override_cf 0.02, fullstop_override_days 5, high_load_pctl 0.85, min_inmerit_hours 6, min_outage_days 1.0, merit_order_guard true; only iso and years differ) -- data/raw/campd-unit-outages-shortgas-SPP.csv, 2,838 windows, 39 plants, 75 units, CC_REGULAR 2,204 / ST_GAS 608 / CC_CHP 26. Zero parameters chosen by the lane, nothing swept. Nested by construction: data/fleet/arrays.py opens the block on unit_outage_short_windows and passes gas_scope inside it, so the gas flag is inert alone and the arm carries BOTH. Screen year 2025 (largest measured footprint, 11,354.227 GWh / 1,063 windows against 2024's 9,297.096 / 840 and 2023's 10,762.570 / 935). MEASURED, one shard, 138 s: the overlay fires at 218 plant-tranches, and the shard's own zero-LP probe of unit_outage_short_derate_factors confirms the gas scope really entered -- 23 plant-groups at gas_scope False vs 55 at True (COAL 23 + CC_REGULAR 18 + ST_GAS 13 + CC_CHP 1), coal unchanged either way. G1/G2/G3 clear (confinement exact; response 3.8175 TWh inside its 9.43 TWh bound). THE KILL: G4 identity FAILS at slack 10,911.0219 MWh in 12 hours, ALL in SPP-South, in three clusters (2025-09-15, 2025-10-06, 2025-12-21), every hour at VOLL $2,000; and G5 FLIPS BOTH load-bearing price criteria PASS -> FAIL (C3a 28.7893 -> 33.1683 = +15.97 % against a +/-10 % band; C3b 0.1638 -> 0.2619 against a 0.20 bar). The entire price move is scarcity, not merit order -- all 18 hours above $200 are exactly $2,000, the slack penalty -- so the arm does not price SPP better, it makes SPP infeasible. THE FAILURE MODE WAS PRE-REGISTERED: PRECOMMIT section 7 named it before the solve ('2,838 gas windows over three years is too many for a merit-order guard to have filtered -- SPP's CC fleet runs at ~49 % CF, and a 1-5 day dead span at that CF can be economics rather than an outage'). PJM's and MISO's K on the coal parent do not carry here and the reason is fleet conduct, not plumbing. THE EXTRACT STAYS COMMITTED -- what is rejected is arming it in SPP's LP, not the data. Evidence: docs/RESULT-spp-32-shortwindow-screen-2026-09-12.md, docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-spp-32-shortwindow-availability-2026-09-12.md, docs/handoffs/SHARDREPORT-spp32-B-2025.md." },
    unit_outage_dispatched_bin_denominator: { cell: "U", ev: "Row added by miso-266 (2026-09-22) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): no MISO verdict crosses the boundary (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]), and the SIZE of the defect is a per-ISO FLEET property \u2014 how far this ISO's dispatched (plant_code, plant_group) capacity departs from outages._iso_plant_capacity's reconstruction of it. THE TRANSFER QUESTION IS ZERO-LP AND WELL-POSED, and is MISO's, reusable verbatim (scripts/probes/_miso266_denominator_vs_lp.py): rebuild this ISO's keeper fleet fleet_only for each registered year, sum pmax per (plant_code, plant_group), and set it beside _iso_plant_capacity(iso). Read three numbers \u2014 (i) how many bins carry denom/cap_LP below 1 (those OVER-remove, and a bin whose flagged units then sum past the clip is zeroed while running), (ii) how many bins the LP dispatches that the reconstructed map LACKS ENTIRELY (those ride un-derated through their own measured outage \u2014 the SPP-48 Oklaunion pathology), and (iii) whether this ISO synthesizes exit-cohort bins at all (fleet/assembly.py's _r{yyyy}{mm} tag fires only where the bins sheet carries Retirement_Year, so an ISO with no mid-window partial-plant exits may find the two maps already agree and the flag inert). An ISO arming unit_outage_lp_capacity_basis or unit_outage_extract_basis_share must disarm it first \u2014 the loaders raise, by rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]. NOTE THE SCOPE before reading any census: the CHP groups (CC_CHP / CT_CHP / ST_CHP) are EXCLUDED by construction \u2014 there cap_LP is the grid-facing residual after the behind-the-meter host steam is held out, so the incumbent nameplate denominator is the correct one and the flag is the identity. A CHP-heavy ratio in this ISO's census is therefore NOT this flag's object." },
    unit_outage_extract_basis_share: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7." },
    unit_outage_window_hour_grain: { cell: "U", ev: "Row added by nyiso-229 (2026-09-12) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): the defect\u0027s SIZE is a per-ISO data property \u2014 how much of each ISO\u0027s day-grain window mass sits at a boundary the detector never detected \u2014 so NYISO\u0027s measurement fills NYISO\u0027s cell only, and a lane adopting it derives its OWN \u0027-perunitmerithour-\u0027 extract from its own CAMPD (no number crosses). The three-step protocol is zero-LP and is NYISO\u0027s, reusable verbatim: (1) count the unit-hours the loader asserts unavailable while the meter shows grossLoad > 0, and split them by distance from the nearest window boundary \u2014 within 23 h is SCHEMA rounding, deeper is DETECTOR misplacement and a different defect; (2) count same-unit day-grain window overlaps and check the histogram is a single 24.0 h bin (the shared-boundary-day fingerprint); (3) check the ISO has tight hours for the restored capacity to reach \u2014 firm-load slack OR a short reserve family \u2014 because a lever that gives capacity back to a market with slack everywhere is inert. Predicated on campd_per_unit_attribution AND campd_outage_merit_order_guard, so an ISO arming neither reads the field as n/a in practice." },
