    unit_outage_netload_mask_repair: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED 2026-09-26 by OWNER RULING, verbatim 'Yes promote rebase merge and give handoff', over the lane's pre-registered HOLD (condition (e): one new D-4 row) -- armed on SPP's designated keeper 2026-09-26-spp-85-netload-mask. SPP-85 SOLVED (2026-09-26; docs/handoffs/RESULT-spp-85-netload-mask-repair-2026-09-26.md; registered 2026-09-26-spp-85-netload-mask, bundle results/calibration/spp85_arm_span): 7 year-shards, control + arm at pinned 0ff620d1, arm vs control coal +1.47/+1.64/+3.80/+3.37/+2.15/+2.92/+3.32 TWh and price -0.23/-0.42/-2.10/-2.28/-0.51/-0.72/-0.89 $/MWh 2019-2025, slack never up. 2023-25 stays CALIBRATED (C3a -5.2/-6.8/-4.2 %); 2021 C3a FAIL -> PASS (+4.4 %); NEW validation FAILs C1 COAL_PRB 2021 +10.31, CC_REGULAR 2021/22 -8.98/-9.72, C4 gas 2021 0.316; C8 2022 ST_GAS 31.5 % grounded; ONE new D-4 row (Holcomb 108 coal_mustrun 2021) -> pre-registered condition (e) FAILS -> recommendation HOLD; zero new DOF. Restored coal over-dispatches vs EIA-923: the over-counted outage was compensating (rule 14 root cause = coal/CC merit order + Holcomb floor). Stays O pending the owner's promotion ruling. Prior: SPP-85 (2026-09-26): BUILT, default off, on SPP's own measurement (docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-85-coal-outage-basis-2026-09-26.md). outage_detect._ISO_TO_BA lacked SPP, so the recorded in-merit filter was inert; the three -netloadmask- companions re-derive each committed extract at its own recorded invocation with the SWPP mask live: standard 6,627 -> 6,581 rows (46 coal), short 1,689 -> 460, partial 204 -> 0. Zero-LP fleet delta on the keeper rspp_span: coal-only, +0.51/0.66/1.04/0.90/0.58/0.84/0.81 GW mean coal availability 2019-2025; every other LP array byte-identical except min_gen (the incumbent coal must-run floor re-applies in restored hours). Closes 22-52 % of the keeper-minus-SPP-published coal excess. Verdict pending the owner-gated 7-year shard solve (PRECOMMIT-spp-85-netload-mask-repair-2026-09-26.md)." },
