    tranche_startup_amortization: { cell: "R", ev: "SPP-83 (2026-09-26, cell UNCHANGED R; ZERO LP; FINDING-spp-83-keeper-clears-on-offline-capacity-2026-09-26.md §2): the SPP commitment-cost source survey was re-run from source for this family's inputs. No public SPP per-class or per-unit start-up/no-load DOLLAR values exist: MMU ASOM 2022-24 publishes fuel-level fleet-average start/min-run/min-down TIMES only (gas unsplit; 2024 gas min-run 21 h, min-down 8 h); Marketplace Protocols App. G gives the mitigated start-cost FORMULA with no values; make-whole/resource-uplift reports are monthly realized-outcome $ by named location (rule-13 inadmissible); EQR has no operating parameters; ITP/PROMOD inputs are proprietary; NREL/APTECH 55433 is national-generic. A start cost only raises offers in a pure LP and never removes MW from the stack, so it is the wrong structure for SPP-82/83's offline-capacity object at any value. SPP MERIT-ORDER (2026-09-07) — R: REFUSED AT PHASE 0 ON ITS OWN ARITHMETIC, ZERO LP SPENT (rule 29 clause 0). Covers v2 tranche_startup_amortization + v3 tranche_startup_measured_runs, the arm as declared in PRECOMMIT-spp-merit-order-2026-09-07.md §3.1; v4 tranche_startup_conditional_runs was never part of it and is untested. ADMISSIBLE, then refused on size — the rule-19 [R-ONE-MECH] enumeration that REFUSED this mechanism on ERCOT (DIAGNOSIS-ercot145-tranche-startup-2026-07-31.md §1: ERCOT CT rows already carried +$13.1/+$34.9/+$292-451 of FITTED multiplier margin against a $2.9-4.0 measured amortization, i.e. stacking) points the OTHER WAY on SPP: every SPP band multiplier is 1.0, so the CT_PEAKER/CT_CHP econ+peak and CC_* peak rows carry an above-SRMC margin of exactly $0.00 — ERCOT-145's own \"four keeper ISOs\" regime. Rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]: SPP's OWN artifact derived and committed by this lane, data/raw/_processed-legacy/campd_ct_run_lengths_SPP.csv (scripts/data/derive_campd_ct_run_lengths.py --iso SPP; 51 facilities / 138 units / 50,460 measured start-to-stop runs, 2023-2025, class-fallback median 9.0 h, per-plant p25 7 / p50 9 / p75 11 h) — SPP CTs run LONGER than every other ISO's measured fleet (NYISO 4, CAISO 4, ERCOT 6, PJM 7, MISO 10 h), which is why the measured markup is small. FOOTPRINT (arm fleet_only rebuild, mc_base byte-identical to the control): 384 rows / 11,600.3-11,630.9 MW gain a start-recovery term — CT_PEAKER econ+peak 10,519-10,566 MW at $20/MW-start over 9 h = MAX $2.140-2.141/MWh cap-weighted, CT_CHP 116-132 MW at $0.66-0.87, CC/CC_CHP peak 949 MW on the v2 P0 basis. GATE G-ROT (threshold INHERITED UNCHANGED from the price-family lane's pre-registered G-2: the steepening ratio MHR(>95pct)/MHR(25-75pct) must RISE >= 10 % of the control): at the arm's MAXIMUM markup the ratio moves 1.5653 -> 1.5676 (+0.147 %), 1.3306 -> 1.3396 (+0.676 %), 1.6665 -> 1.6833 (+1.008 %) in 2023/2024/2025 — a STOP by 10-68x — while the level moves the WRONG WAY (LW mean x1.0230 / x1.0228 / x1.0188 on a model already too dear). Granting the un-computable CC-peak leg a generous 9 h (or punitive 4 h) horizon turns rotation NEGATIVE in two of three years (-0.588/-0.135/+0.696 %; -0.952/-0.443/+2.016 %), so the refusal is robust to that limitation, not dependent on it. Graded on a re-clearing predictor VALIDATED against the price-family lane's SOLVED 2025 arm (LP-measured LW -9.05 % vs predicted -8.11/-9.12 %; LP-measured rotation +0.52 % vs predicted +2.09 %, i.e. the instrument OVER-STATES rotation ~4x — reported against interest, and it can only make the gate easier). No LP, no bundle, no registration; keeper 2026-09-07-spp-3-screened-input unchanged. Record: docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-merit-order-2026-09-07.md §4.2." },
