    coal_prb_proxy_own_iso: { cell: "O", ev: "OPEN, and SPP is AFFECTED TODAY. Measured by NWPP-41 (zero LP, not an SPP solve): the ERCOT-pooled PRB proxy currently reaches 3 non-reporting SPP PRB plants in 2023/2024 (10862, 54211, 57046) and 5 in 2025 (adding 2240 and 6193 \u2014 6193 Harrington being the very plant SPP-62 chased through the census). NOT FIXED HERE \u2014 rule 25 / rule 28(d). Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-nwpp-41-2026-09-17.md \u00a73." },
    campd_outage_windows: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-85 (2026-09-26): ROOT CAUSE of SPP-84's coal over-count found in CODE -- outage_detect._ISO_TO_BA had no SPP key, so the committed SPP extracts' recorded in-merit filter never ran (every span kept). The -netloadmask- re-derivation (field unit_outage_netload_mask_repair, O) removes 0.57-1.12 GW of the 1.18-3.40 GW excess vs SPP's published coal outage (short 1,689->460, partial 204->0, standard -46 coal windows); a winter-heavy residual 0.6-2.5 GW remains in >=5-day dead stops (successor: campd_outage_merit_order_guard on the per-unit family). SPP's own RC Outage Coordination Methodology s3.2.1 books Reserve Shutdown as a CROW Planned Outage, so the 'SPP excludes reserve shutdowns' premise is unsupported. Cell stays U (the incumbent layer's verdict is carried by the repair field's cell). SPP-84 (2026-09-26, ZERO LP, cell NOT moved -- stays U; docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-84-published-outage-vs-keeper-2026-09-26.md): the keeper (outage_source historic, data/raw/campd-unit-outages-SPP.csv, >=5-day windows, min_inmerit_hours 24) carries MORE COAL OUTAGE than SPP publishes (capacity-of-generation-on-outage) in every year, +1.18/+2.56/+2.59/+2.40/+2.31/+3.40 GW 2019-24, winter-heavy (2020 Jan/Feb +4.2/+4.0; 2024 Feb +9.4) -- the signature of economic reserve shutdowns admitted as outages by a lax in-merit filter; consistent with SPP-83 keeper coal available BELOW SPP coal ONLINE. Gas windows cover CC/ST only; CT_PEAKER has none. Named successor: a zero-LP unit-level coal-window reconciliation against the published series, then (owner-gated) a deriver-scope change under rule 23 on the measured-source basis. Prior: SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7." },
