    unit_outage_short_windows: { cell: "K", ev: "2026-09-25 (R-SPP): the second shape unit_partial_outage_windows is now IN THE KEEPER (2026-09-24-r-spp-corrected-inputs, promoted on the owner ruling 'Yes promote'); cell stays K. R-SPP (2026-09-24; run 2026-09-24-r-spp-corrected-inputs, bundle results/calibration/rspp_span 2019-2025, NOT REGISTERED ON main pending the owner's promotion ruling -- an unpromoted registration trips audit_keepers E13; PRECOMMIT docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-r-spp-2019-2025-inputs-2026-09-24.md (ec13e5c2, pushed before any shard); RESULT docs/handoffs/RESULT-r-spp-2019-2025-inputs-2026-09-24.md): TESTED BY SOLVE ON ALL SEVEN YEARS, one shard per year (rule 36), incumbent hydro-5 recipe + all five measured_*_heat_rates + unit_partial_outage_windows + mid_vintage_exit_carry + eia860_vintage_tracks_solve_year, on the F1 artifacts (pooled 2019-2025 + per-year rows) and F2 extracts; offer multipliers unchanged. 2023-25 span-restricted: CALIBRATED -> CALIBRATED (C3c ledgered caveat, unchanged). 2019-22: NOT-YET -> NOT-YET, same failing set; C3a 2019/2020/2021 +7.9/+15.5/+1.9 -> +13.3/+21.2/+10.0 % (2019, 2021 PASS->FAIL), C3b 2021/2022 FAIL->PASS (0.234->0.132, 0.208->0.182), C1 COAL_PRB 2022 +9.60 -> +9.58 TWh (still the only gated C1 FAIL). Cell stays K (short-coal shape, keeper). ITS SECOND SHAPE unit_partial_outage_windows (unit-grain partial derate, F2 extract campd-partial-outages-SPP.csv, 17-41 windows/yr) ARMED on all seven years: O, owner has not ruled; coal availability -0.52 to -1.28 TWh/yr; C8/D-4 clean. --- SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7. ANNOTATED AND MOVED U -> O by SPP-32 (2026-09-12): SCREENED on 2025 and NOT adjudicated -- promotion is the OWNER'S act (the posture SPP-52a's producing lane set). The extract had existed committed and UNARMED since it was derived (data/raw/campd-unit-outages-short-SPP.csv, 620 windows, 24 plants, 39 units, 620/620 rows plant_group COAL); keeper 9 carries unit_outage_short_windows=False. Screen year 2025, named in the PRECOMMIT on this mechanism's own largest measured footprint (7,050.714 GWh removed capacity-hours / 246 windows, against 2024's 6,446.563 / 211 and 2023's 5,174.373 / 163), never on a residual (rule 29(1)). Control = keeper 9's COMMITTED bundle differenced, NO control solve (rule 29(b) form 4; the G-DRIFT audit classified all six changed solve-path files between basis_sha 09d9fc00 and the pinned base as INERT). MEASURED, one shard, 202 s: the overlay FIRES -- 'short unit-outage derate (SPP 2025): 94 plant-tranches derated' -- and removes COAL 2.5714 TWh (COAL_PRB 80.4149 -> 78.0526, COAL_LIGNITE 6.7981 -> 6.5890) which lands almost entirely on gas (+2.3710 TWh). FOUR OF FIVE PRE-REGISTERED GATES CLEAR: G1 direction PASS, G2 confinement PASS (23 COAL plant-groups; no gas/CT/VRE availability moved), G3 magnitude 2.5714 < 3.857 TWh bound PASS, G5 no non-target load-bearing flip PASS (C3a +0.66 % -> +5.15 %, still inside +/-10 %; C3b 0.1638 -> 0.1878, still inside 0.20; every 2025 C1 row and all of C2 are SKIPPED by the scorer on the preliminary EIA-923 vintage, so G5 reduces to C3a/C3b on this year). G4 IDENTITY FAILS AS WRITTEN: slack 240.5966 MWh in 2 hours in SPP-South at VOLL, against a gate demanding 0.0000. THE GATE IS DEFECTIVE AND THE LANE SAYS SO RATHER THAN REWRITING IT: keeper 9's OWN committed span carries a LARGER slack event -- 370.1017 MWh, 2 hours, SPP-South, VOLL, in 2024 (2023 and 2025 are 0.0000) -- so 'slack stays 0.0000' is a standard the designated keeper does not meet, and SPP-32 generalised a one-year accident into a gate. Re-reading a pre-registered gate after seeing its number is the fitted-mechanism selection rule 1 [R-STRUCT](c) forbids, so the arm is STOPPED and the defect is reported to the owner instead. Zero free parameters (ledger stays 3/2); offer_curve_by_group byte-identical at a uniform 0.93. The full span was NOT spent. Evidence: docs/RESULT-spp-32-shortwindow-screen-2026-09-12.md, docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-spp-32-shortwindow-availability-2026-09-12.md, docs/handoffs/SHARDREPORT-spp32-A-2025.md. PROMOTED O -> K by SPP-36 (2026-09-12) ON THE OWNER'S IN-SESSION RULING (\"Is this a recommended keeper candidate? If so plz promote. If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper.\"): the full 2023-2025 span, ONE replay_keeper invocation, 377 s, is SPP's TENTH KEEPER 2026-09-12-spp-36-shortwindow-span. MEASURED across the span: 80 / 73 / 94 plant-tranches derated; coal -2.0273 / -2.3736 / -3.1775 TWh onto gas +2.0283 / +2.3764 / +3.1807, energy conserved to <= 0.0032 TWh; load-weighted price 25.3716 -> 25.7428, 25.4676 -> 26.0214, 28.7893 -> 29.5377. DETERMINATION CALIBRATED, grade 7 of 8, 0 FAILS, 1 ledgered C3c caveat, free-class C1 16/16 / 12/12 -- the same shape as keeper 9 on every scored criterion. C3a +2.44 / +3.54 / +5.15 % and C3b 0.1760 / 0.1658 / 0.1878 both degrade on two years (2024's C3b IMPROVES) and all six stay in band. THE SLACK COST IS ZERO: 0.0000 / 370.1017 / 0.0000 MWh in BOTH arm and control -- 2024's event is the keeper's own pre-existing one and the arm adds no unserved energy; dump 0.0000 everywhere; hours > $200 move only in 2024, 5 -> 7 against 59 actual. THE SCREEN'S SLACK FIGURES DID NOT SURVIVE THE SPAN, AND THE REASON IS A PARENT DESIGN ERROR, NOT A MODEL EFFECT: three single-year fan-out shards reported 1295.6995 MWh (2024) and 240.5966 (2025) of added slack, but those differenced SINGLE-YEAR arm solves against a SPAN-solved control. The span-vs-span A/B, where arm and control share construction, is the valid one and is what is registered (rule 16 [R-ALLYEARS] admits a single-year solve only as a throwaway probe). 2023 -- first year in both constructions -- reproduces to 4 dp; 2024 and 2025 do not, and whether SPP's solve carries process-order sensitivity is OPEN and ROUTED (SPP-27 already recorded reconstruct_bundle_fleet as order-dependent across years within a process for SPP); the A/B is unaffected either way because both legs are 3-year invocations. RULE 21 [R-DOF]: ONE entry added, identified MEASURED-PHYSICAL, not residual -- ledger 5 / 3 against the control's OWN config rebuilt at HEAD (4 / 3), so n_residual is UNCHANGED; keeper 9's committed 3 / 2 was stale. offer_curve_by_group BYTE-IDENTICAL, SHA-256 090abd793b5fa5a79b3e6102d5443585f44a3e6ddcdc264ea1f83be46ba62f65 in both legs. Rule 23: the extract was NOT re-derived. CARRIED, NOT ABSORBED: D-4 still FAILS 12 rows of 71, every one st_gas_mustrun_per_plant x ST_GAS, identical to keeper 9 and unrelated to this COAL scope; D-1/D-2/D-5/D-9/D-10 PASS with non-zero row counts (25/15/8/5/6), checked because an earlier parent-side composition produced VACUOUS zero-row passes. Evidence: docs/RESULT-spp-36-shortwindow-span-2026-09-12.md, docs/handoffs/SHARDREPORT-spp36-span.md, docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-spp-36-shortwindow-span-2026-09-12.md." },
