    hydro_level_923_hy: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7. --- BENCHMARK COMPLEMENT LANDED 2026-09-12 (gov-hydro-seam-1, the cross-ISO governance session pjm-h1 escalated to; docs/FINDING-gov-hydro-seam-1-2026-09-12.md, docs/PRECOMMIT-gov-hydro-seam-1-2026-09-12.md + its vintage-fallthrough ADDENDUM). THE CELL DOES NOT MOVE AND NO MECHANISM WAS TESTED \u2014 this is a BENCHMARK construction repair, the other end of the same comparison this cell pins the MODEL end of, and it arms nothing. ZERO LP. Two changes, both shared ISO-agnostic code: (1) plant_taxonomy.classify_plant now returns OTHER for prime mover PS before the fuel == WAT test \u2014 366 EIA-923 rows 2019-2026, every one WAT/PS, none of any other kind; (2) run_calibration_full._backfill_renewables_eia930 refuses the EIA-930 NG:WAT swap for hydro when the ISO-year is PS-folded AND its own EIA-923 HY census is complete (_hydro_benchmark_is_923_only), so a folded year is scored on the conventional-only population its LP units are. NOT SOLVE-AFFECTING, MEASURED: zero dominant-class flips reach a gas class so the ERCOT bin override and mixed_fossil_plants are byte-identical; the injected OTHER must-run moves 0.000000 MWh in all 42 scored ISO-years (the dead _pumped_storage_plant_ids guard goes live and holds exactly those rows back out, with ZERO over-filter rows); zero solve-surface rows move and check_cache_key_registration is clean. GATE-NEUTRAL, MEASURED ACROSS THE WHOLE REGISTRY: all seven keepers hold CALIBRATED and ALL 47 REGISTERED RUNS score byte-identically, control vs arm \u2014 every criterion, every caveat, every determination. THIS ISO'S HYDRO ACTUAL MOVES: NOT folded; decision 2 alone: 2023 8.3472->8.4002 (+0.0530) | 2024 8.6543->8.7018 (+0.0475) | 2025 0.0000 (swap fires). THE COMMITTED BENCH PARTS ARE NOT YET REGENERATED and still carry the OLD actual: the committed bundles are SLIM (dispatch/ is gitignored and absent), so a bench render needs a re-solve, and spending ~40 shard-years of LP on a gate-neutral display number was refused. Each ISO's next registration refreshes its own parts automatically and the move above is what it will show \u2014 already scored, flips nothing. REPORTED, NOT ABSORBED: check_bench_freshness cannot see this (run_calibration_full.py is not in bench_stamp.PAYLOAD_SOURCES) and reads 0 STALE / 'reproduces at HEAD' for parts whose hydro row does not; the gap is escalated in the FINDING \u00a76, not unilaterally closed." },
    hydro_vintage_input_repair: { cell: "K", ev: "SPP-42 (2026-09-07) — K: KEEPER, armed on 2026-09-07-spp-2-crosswalk-hydro (bundle spp42_crosswalk_B; docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-42-2026-09-07.md §2-§3). The pair --hydro-backfill-year 2024 --hydro-eia930-monthly, applied to every year (rule 22: a measured input is never held out): the EIA-923 preliminary 2025 vintage carried 0.0233 TWh of SPP hydro (1 plant) against the measured EIA-930 NG:WAT 8.8299 TWh; 21 plants backfilled from 2024 and the monthly level pinned; 2023 / 2024 re-pinned 8.4003 -> 8.3441 / 8.7023 -> 8.9731 TWh. Zero-LP prediction (build_hydro_fleet) reproduced exactly by the solve (8.82 TWh dispatched). Rule-29(a) 2025 screen: unserved 2,007 MWh in 6 h -> 89.3 MWh in 1 h (100 % of the North cleared, 91 % of the South); the charter gate's literal unserved->0 leg NOT met and the lane proceeded on rule 14 (stated, FINDING §2.3). Differenced against the spp-1 control: C3a-2025 +21.7 % -> +7.2 %, C3b-2025 0.283 -> 0.189, coal/CC/CT/ST 2025 -2.4 / -2.0 / -2.7 / -1.7 TWh. A rule-14 INPUT correction with zero free parameters, not a lever. Also found by this lane and ROUTED (P9): EIA-930 SWPP Demand carries stuck identical-value runs (2025: 698 h in 19 runs, longest 155 h from 2025-12-15; 2024: 396 h; 2023: 36 h) that the 2.5x spike screen cannot see." },
